# WRESTLING

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

This document defines the physiological, biomechanical, technical and tactical demands of Wrestling.

Its purpose is to enable the Combat Athlete System (CAS) to understand the unique performance profile of wrestlers and to individualize physical preparation accordingly.

This document describes performance requirements.

It does not prescribe training methods.

---

# Definition

Wrestling is a grappling combat sport in which athletes attempt to control, throw or pin their opponent through superior positioning, leverage and force production.

Success depends upon:

Position.

Balance.

Leverage.

Timing.

Strength.

Conditioning.

Technical execution.

---

# Philosophy

Wrestling is a sport of constant physical engagement.

Every exchange is a contest for position.

Victory rarely belongs to the strongest athlete alone.

It belongs to the athlete who best combines force, technique, leverage and relentless work capacity.

